    { q: "Could the money have floated here?", a: "“Not for years. Rubber bands rot in river water. If these bundles had drifted a long time, they'd have fallen apart.”", clue: "banded" },
    { q: "Which rivers could carry it here?", a: "“The Lewis River joins the Columbia below this beach, downstream. Water doesn't flow uphill. The Washougal joins above it, upstream.”", clue: "rivers" },
    { q: "Could someone have buried it?", a: "“Sure. A person with a shovel could have put it here. I can't prove that, and I can't rule it out.”", clue: "buried" },
    { q: "Did the dredging bring it?", a: "“Maybe. The 1974 dredge spread river-bottom sand right on this beach. Ask a geologist about the layers.”", clue: "dredge" }
  ],
