    { q: "Could you make that jump?", a: "“At night, in freezing sleet, over trees? I've made hundreds of jumps and I wouldn't. Not impossible, but very hard.”", clue: "night" },
    { q: "What was he wearing?", a: "“A suit, a raincoat and street shoes. Every skydiver I know would wear boots, a jumpsuit and a helmet.”", clue: "clothes" },
    { q: "Does his parachute choice tell you anything?", a: "“He took the older military chute, which is harder to steer, over the better sport one. And the reserve he grabbed was a dummy, sewn shut.”", clue: "chute" },
    { q: "Was his plan smart?", a: "“The plan was clever. Four chutes so nobody could hand him a bad one. Low and slow with the stairs ready. Whoever he was, he'd thought about this.”", clue: "planner" }
