:: Start [nobar]
<div class="stamp">Case file 001</div>
<p class="meta">FBI Portland Office · February 1980</p>
<h1>The Tena Bar Riddle</h1>
<p>It's been more than eight years since the man called D.B. Cooper jumped from Flight 305. The case has gone cold. Then the phone rings.</p>
<p class="quote">"A family on a Columbia River beach called Tena Bar was digging to make a campfire. Their eight-year-old, Brian, found bundles of old twenty-dollar bills in the sand. Get down there. I need to know: is it Cooper's money, how did it get there, and is Cooper alive or dead? Seven leads."</p>
<div class="how">
<p><b>How to investigate</b></p>
<ul>
<li>Visiting a new place uses one lead. Going back is free.</li>
<li>Interviews: two questions each.</li>
<li>Some clues point toward "he survived," some toward "he didn't," and some don't decide anything. You'll see which at the end.</li>
<li><b>This case has no answer key.</b> "We can't tell yet" is a real verdict if your evidence points both ways.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<div class="actions">[[Start investigating|Hub]]</div>


:: Hub
<<if $leads lte 0>><<goto "OutOfLeads">><</if>>
<<set _ev to setup.events.filter(function(e){ return $leads <= e.at && !$events.includes(e.id); })>>
<<for _e range _ev>><<run $events.push(_e.id)>>
<<if _e.kind is "headline">><div class="headline"><span class="paper">The Oregonian</span><<print _e.text>></div>
<<else>><p class="quote chief"><<print _e.text>></p><</if>>
<</for>>
