</ul>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Deduction board (free)">><<set $return to "Hub">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[I'm ready to give my verdict|Accusation]]</div>


:: OutOfLeads
<h2>Out of leads</h2>
<p class="quote chief">"That's all the time we have," your supervisor says. "What's your verdict?"</p>
<div class="actions"><<link "One last look at the deduction board">><<set $return to "OutOfLeads">><<goto "Board">><</link>>[[Give my verdict|Accusation]]</div>


:: Beach
<h2>Tena Bar</h2>
<p>A wide, sandy beach on the Columbia River, cold wind off the water. The Ingram family shows you the shallow hole where Brian was smoothing out sand for a campfire. Agents with shovels and sifting screens are already combing the beach.</p>
<p>Three crumbly bundles of twenty-dollar bills sit in evidence bags. You can still read some of the serial numbers.</p>
<<clue "bundles">>
<<clue "place">>
<<tomap>>


:: Lab
<h2>The FBI lab</h2>
<p>An agent lines the soggy bills up against a printout of the 1971 microfilm list, one serial number at a time.</p>
<p class="quote">"They match. This is the ransom. And here's the strange part: banks across the country have had this list for nine years, and not one of these bills has ever turned up anywhere else."</p>
<<clue "match">>
<<clue "unspent">>
<<tomap>>


:: Geologist
<h2>A geologist's office</h2>
<p>A geologist, Dr. Leonard Palmer, has dug careful trenches at Tena Bar and drawn the layers of sand like a cake.</p>
<p class="quote">"Down here is the clay and sand the dredge dumped in 1974. The money was sitting above it, with more layers of river sand in between. So the money got here after 1974. It didn't come with the dredge."</p>
<<clue "layers">>
<<clue "dredge">>
<<tomap>>


:: River
<h2>Interview: a river scientist</h2>
<p>A river scientist who studies how the Columbia moves sand and logs meets you on the beach with a map of the river and everything that flows into it.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "river">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "river">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: Skydiver
<h2>Interview: a skydiving instructor</h2>
<p>An instructor at a local skydiving school has followed the Cooper case for years. She has opinions.</p>
<div id="ans"><<pastanswers "skydiver">></div>
<div id="iv"><<interview "skydiver">></div>
<<tomap>>


:: Weather
<h2>The weather bureau</h2>
<p>A clerk pulls the records for the night of November 24, 1971, along the flight path.</p>
<<clue "weather">>
<<tomap>>


:: Files
<h2>The old 1971 search files</h2>
<p>Boxes of maps marked with grid squares. In 1971, searchers walked the forest near Ariel and Lake Merwin, square by square.</p>
<p class="quote">"Mud, steep hills, endless trees," an agent says. "No parachute. No money. No body."</p>
<<clue "nothing">>
<p>Clipped to the last box is a newer note.</p>
<<clue "placard">>
<<tomap>>


:: Newsroom
<h2>The newspaper office</h2>
<p>The Cooper story is back on every front page, and everyone has a theory.</p>
<p class="quote">"He's on a beach in Mexico, spending it," says one reporter. "No way," says another. "That beach is his grave."</p>
<<clue "rich">>
<<clue "dead">>
<<tomap>>


