:: Verdict [nobar]
<<set _lean to function(id){ var c = setup.cards[id]; return c.type === "deduction" ? c.leans : c.type; }>>
<<set _pins to $pinned.map(_lean)>>
<<set _nS to _pins.filter(function(x){ return x === "survived"; }).length>>
<<set _nD to _pins.filter(function(x){ return x === "didnt"; }).length>>
<<set _nA to _pins.filter(function(x){ return x === "assumption"; }).length>>
<<set _nb to $notebook.map(_lean)>>
<<set _haveS to _nb.includes("survived")>>
<<set _haveD to _nb.includes("didnt")>>
<<if $verdict is "survived">><<set _s1 to _nS gte 2 and _nA is 0>>
<<elseif $verdict is "didnt">><<set _s1 to _nD gte 2 and _nA is 0>>
<<else>><<set _s1 to _nS gte 1 and _nD gte 1 and _nA is 0>><</if>>
<<if $verdict is "unknown">><<set _s2 to $conf isnot "very">>
<<elseif $conf is "very">><<set _s2 to false>>
<<elseif $conf is "fairly">><<set _s2 to _s1>>
<<else>><<set _s2 to true>><</if>>
<<if $verdict is "survived">><<set _s3 to _haveD>><<elseif $verdict is "didnt">><<set _s3 to _haveS>><<else>><<set _s3 to _haveS and _haveD>><</if>>
<<set $stars to (_s1 ? 1 : 0) + (_s2 ? 1 : 0) + (_s3 ? 1 : 0)>>
<<set $deductions to $notebook.filter(function(id){ return setup.cards[id].type === "deduction"; }).length>>
<<switch $verdict>>
<<case "survived">><div class="stamp">Verdict: survived</div>
<<case "didnt">><div class="stamp">Verdict: didn't survive</div>
<<default>><div class="stamp solved">Verdict: can't tell yet</div>
<</switch>>
<h2>Detective rating: <<print $stars>> of 3 stars</h2>
<p class="meta">Nobody knows the true answer, so these stars measure how well you used evidence, not whether you "won."</p>
<ul class="stars">
<li @class="_s1 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s1 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Evidence that fits your verdict.</b> <<if _s1>>The cards you pinned back up what you said.<<elseif _nA gt 0>>You pinned a newspaper guess. Guesses aren't evidence.<<elseif $verdict is "unknown">>For "can't tell yet," pin at least one card pointing each way.<<else>>Pin at least two cards that point toward your verdict.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s2 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s2 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Confidence that fits the evidence.</b> <<if $conf is "very" and $verdict isnot "unknown">>The evidence points both ways, so "very sure" is too sure.<<elseif $verdict is "unknown" and $conf is "very">>Interesting: very sure that nobody can tell? Fair, but try "fairly sure."<<elseif _s2>>Your confidence matches how strong your evidence is.<<else>>"Fairly sure" needs pinned evidence that backs you up. Otherwise it's a hunch.<</if>></li>
<li @class="_s3 ? 'on' : 'off'"><span aria-hidden="true"><<print _s3 ? '★' : '☆'>></span> <b>Looked at the other side.</b> <<if _s3>>You collected evidence pointing the other way, too.<<else>>You never found a clue pointing the other way. Good detectives look for evidence that could prove them wrong.<</if>></li>
</ul>
<p class="meta">Deductions worked out: <<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></p>
<h3>Your notebook, flipped over</h3>
<<if $notebook.length is 0>><p class="note">You didn't collect any cards.</p><<else>>
<div class="cards reveal"><<for _id range $notebook>><<set _t to _lean(_id)>><div @class="'card ' + _t"><span class="tag"><<print setup.cards[_id].type === "deduction" ? "Deduction · " + setup.typeLabel[_t] : setup.typeLabel[_t]>></span><span class="card-title"><<print setup.cards[_id].title>></span><<if $pinned.includes(_id)>><span class="pinned-mark">You pinned this</span><</if>></div><</for>></div><</if>>
<div class="actions">[[What really happened|RealHistory]]</div>


:: RealHistory [nobar]
<h2>What really happened</h2>
<p>The beach money was the only ransom money ever found. The geologist's sand layers showed it arrived after the 1974 dredging, and nobody has ever explained exactly how it got there.</p>
<p>The FBI looked at more than 800 suspects. Many agents believed Cooper didn't survive the jump: the weather, his clothes and his parachute choice were all against him, and the money was never spent. But no body or parachute was ever found. In 2016, after 45 years, the FBI stopped actively working the case.</p>
<p>The search hasn't stopped. In 2017, volunteer scientists found tiny bits of rare metals, like pure titanium, on Cooper's clip-on tie. Back in 1971, metals like that were used in only a few kinds of factories, such as aircraft plants. Maybe that's a clue to his job. Maybe the tie was secondhand.</p>
<div class="lesson">
<h3>Your lesson as a trainee</h3>
<ul>
<li>A new clue can answer one question and raise three more.</li>
<li>Your confidence should be only as strong as your evidence.</li>
<li>"We can't tell yet" is an honest answer, not a failure.</li>
</ul>
</div>
<p class="note">Made up for this game: the river scientist, the skydiving instructor, and the interview wording. Everything else is based on the real case.</p>
<div class="actions">[[Finish case|CaseClosed]]</div>


:: CaseClosed [nobar]
<<run setup.reportResult()>>
<div class="stamp solved big">Case closed</div>
<h2>Case 001, Part 2 complete</h2>
<p>Detective rating: <b><<print $stars>> of 3</b>. Deductions: <b><<print $deductions>> of <<print setup.dedTotal>></b>.</p>
<p>Tell Rocky your verdict, how sure you were, and which clues convinced you.</p>
<div class="actions secondary"><<link "Play again">><<run Engine.restart()>><</link>></div>
